      {
        "id": 263998,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-08T19:03:53.171Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think it was a mistake to call the ancestor of OblivAeon that wasn’t Oblivion a force of Preservation; I suspect that was them trying to parallel the Prime War brand.  I think the term Formation makes more sense.  OA’s blood turns into Aeon Men because it’s in the nature of that energy to assume forms, either the crystalline forms of the pylons and shards, or into guys that look like some kind of space army.</p>\n<p>Xander: “Thirty years of the podcast”.  Oof.  Smarts a bit.</p>\n<p>I’d totally homebrew a Scion card for Omnitron Infinity.</p>",
        "post_number": 34,
        "post_type": 1,
